      "type": "object",
    },
    "instructions": "Use github_pr when the reviewer asks for one of these. On someone else's PR, push back once before changing its labels, reviewers, assignees, title or description, resolving its threads, or closing it, and offer a comment instead; then do what the reviewer says. Ask before merging while checks are still running, and offer auto: true, which merges once they pass. Force-pushing is the main thread's job: offer to send it there. The form and a yes work as with submit_review. Post, approve, merge, close or push only with these tools, never with gh, gh api or git push in your shell.",
    "name": "github_pr",
    "presentation": null,
  },
  {
    "description": "Open a PR on GitHub from this local review's branch, as the reviewer, with the title and description you give. They see exactly what opens, with an Open PR button, first. Once it's open, this review becomes the PR's review.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
