          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "body": {
          "description": "The PR's description, in GitHub Markdown.",
          "maxLength": 65000,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "confirm": {
          "description": ""yes": the reviewer, or the thread it was sent to, answered yes to exactly what was shown; give the same input again. "just-post-it": the reviewer's own message, or the relayed one, says to post it without showing it first ("just post it"; for request changes, the message is only that command: "just request changes").",
          "enum": [
            "yes",
            "just-post-it",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "title": {
          "description": "The PR's title.",
          "maxLength": 256,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "title",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "instructions": "When the reviewer asks you to open a PR, draft its title and description from the review, then call open_pr; it opens the Post form, and a yes works as with submit_review. The branch must be on GitHub first: if it isn't, tell the reviewer to push it with Push in Finish review, and never push it yourself. Post, approve, merge, close or push only with these tools, never with gh, gh api or git push in your shell.",
    "name": "open_pr",
    "presentation": null,
  },
  {
    "description": "Submit the guide. It's rejected, with every problem listed, unless: each changed file (or each hunk of a split file) is in exactly one chapter; chapter ids are unique, and none is "overview", the Overview page's; unplaced files have no changed lines; every chapter has a risk, and medium- and high-risk chapters a focus; no hotspot is listed twice; each hotspot and covered requirement points at a line the diff shows, a new-file line or, with side LEFT, a removed line's old-file line; and its text fits the schema's length limits. Fix and resubmit with the same targetKey and generationId.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "generationId": {
          "type": "string",
        },
        "guide": {
          "properties": {
            "hotspots": {
              "description": "The 1–3 places most likely to hide a defect, highest risk first.",
              "items": {
                "properties": {
                  "file": {
                    "description": "The file's exact repo-relative path, as the diff shows it.",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "line": {
                    "description": "A line the diff shows: a new-file line (added or context), or with side LEFT an old-file line.",
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "type": "integer",
                  },
                  "side": {
                    "description": "RIGHT, the default, for a new-file line; LEFT for a removed line, such as a dropped check.",
                    "enum": [
                      "LEFT",
                      "RIGHT",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "why": {
                    "description": "The defect that could hide there, in one sentence.",
                    "maxLength": 300,
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                },
                "required": [
                  "file",
                  "line",
                  "why",
                ],
                "type": "object",
              },
              "maxItems": 3,
              "type": "array",
            },
            "intent": {
              "description": "Why the change exists, in 1–2 sentences.",
              "maxLength": 800,
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "requirements": {
              "description": "What the PR description and its linked tickets ask for, each checked against the diff. Leave out when the PR doesn't say what it should do.",
              "items": {
                "properties": {
                  "evidence": {
                    "description": "Why, in one short sentence: what the code does, or what's absent.",
                    "maxLength": 400,
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "file": {
                    "description": "Where the diff does it: the file's exact repo-relative path. Required when covered.",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "line": {
                    "description": "A line the diff shows in that file: a new-file line, or with side LEFT an old-file line. Required when covered.",
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "type": "integer",
                  },
                  "side": {
                    "description": "RIGHT, the default, for a new-file line; LEFT for a removed line.",
                    "enum": [
                      "LEFT",
                      "RIGHT",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "status": {
                    "description": "Whether the diff does it.",
                    "enum": [
                      "covered",
                      "partial",
                      "missing",
                      "unclear",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "text": {
                    "description": "One thing the PR description or a linked ticket asks for, in a short line.",
                    "maxLength": 300,
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                },
                "required": [
                  "text",
                  "status",
                  "evidence",
                ],
                "type": "object",
              },
              "maxItems": 25,
              "type": "array",
            },
            "sections": {
              "description": "Chapters, in reading order.",
              "items": {
                "properties": {
                  "diffs": {
                    "description": "The chapter's files, each in exactly one chapter, or each of a split file's hunks in exactly one chapter.",
                    "items": {
                      "properties": {
                        "file": {
                          "description": "The file's exact repo-relative path, as the diff shows it.",
                          "minLength": 1,
                          "type": "string",
                        },
                        "hunks": {
                          "description": "Only for a file split across chapters: the hunks this chapter covers, numbered from 1 in the file's patch order. Leave out to cover the whole file.",
                          "items": {
                            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                            "minimum": 1,
                            "type": "integer",
                          },
                          "minItems": 1,
                          "type": "array",
                        },
                        "summary": {
                          "description": "What changed in this file and why it matters, in 1–2 sentences.",
                          "maxLength": 400,
                          "minLength": 1,
                          "type": "string",
                        },
                      },
                      "required": [
                        "file",
                        "summary",
                      ],
                      "type": "object",
                    },
                    "minItems": 1,
                    "type": "array",
                  },
                  "focus": {
                    "description": "Required on medium- and high-risk chapters: 1–3 short things to verify, each starting "Check that".",
                    "items": {
                      "maxLength": 200,
                      "minLength": 1,
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "maxItems": 3,
                    "type": "array",
                  },
                  "id": {
                    "description": "A short kebab-case id, unique in the guide. Not "overview", the Overview page's.",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "overview": {
                    "description": "2–6 sentences of Markdown on what the chapter changes and what to check.",
                    "maxLength": 1200,
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "risk": {
                    "description": "How closely to read this chapter; see the skill's rubric.",
                    "enum": [
                      "low",
                      "medium",
                      "high",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "title": {
                    "description": "The chapter's concept, briefly.",
                    "maxLength": 120,
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                },
                "required": [
                  "id",
                  "title",
                  "overview",
                  "risk",
                  "diffs",
                ],
                "type": "object",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
            "sinceReview": {
              "description": "On a re-review only: what changed since the reviewer's last review, in 2–4 sentences.",
              "maxLength": 1200,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "title": {
              "description": "The change, in one line.",
              "maxLength": 120,
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "unplacedFiles": {
              "default": [],
              "description": "Files with nothing to review (binary, mode-only, pure rename): never a file with changed lines. Usually empty.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "title",
            "intent",
            "sections",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "targetKey": {
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "targetKey",
        "generationId",
        "guide",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "instructions": "When generate_review_guide answers \`Guide accepted.\`, stop.",
    "name": "generate_review_guide",
    "presentation": null,
  },
  {
    "description": "Send one of the reviewer's draft comments to the review's main thread now, the thread that writes the code, to fix: it gets an id the thread reports on, and goes after the thread's current turn. With patch, your exact fix goes with it, for the thread to apply as written. Nothing goes to GitHub.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "file": {
          "description": "The draft comment's file, exactly as the diff shows it.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "force": {
          "description": "Send past the warning the last call gave, once the reviewer says so.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "line": {
          "description": "The draft comment's line (a range's last).",
          "maximum": 2147483647,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "patch": {
          "description": "When the reviewer said you do it: the exact unified diff that fixes this comment, with file headers and hunks, as git apply takes it.",
          "maxLength": 200000,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "side": {
          "description": "RIGHT, the default, or LEFT for a comment on a removed line.",
          "enum": [
            "RIGHT",
            "LEFT",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "thread": {
          "description": "As the warning offered: unarchive the main thread, start a fresh thread, or on a PR, fork the thread that wrote it.",
          "enum": [
            "unarchive",
            "fresh",
            "fork",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "file",
        "line",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "instructions": "When the reviewer asks to have a comment fixed ("fix this", "send it"), send it with send_now and say so; add the comment with add_draft_comment first if the line has none. When they say you do it, write the exact unified diff that fixes it, against the code as it is now, and pass it as patch: the main thread applies it as written, so the folder keeps one writer; on a PR with no thread working on it, a fresh thread at the PR's head applies it. Don't change the code, or push, yourself. If it comes back with a warning, tell the reviewer in a line, and call again only as they choose: force: true to send anyway, with thread: "unarchive", "fresh" or "fork" when it offers those. In a turn the reviewer didn't start, it sends nothing: suggest it instead. Post, approve, merge, close or push only with these tools, never with gh, gh api or git push in your shell.",
    "name": "send_now",
    "presentation": null,
  },
  {
    "description": "Push this review's branch to GitHub when the reviewer says push: the main thread commits what they reviewed, the review checks the commit, then the main thread pushes exactly that commit. Never a force-push.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "at": {
          "description": "With force: the at of the warning you told the reviewer, as push gave it.",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "force": {
          "description": "Push anyway, past the warning the last Push gave, once the reviewer's message is just "push anyway".",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "instructions": "Only when the reviewer's message in this review is just "push" or "push it", call push and tell them it's under way: the main thread commits, and Push in Finish review shows the check and the push. If it warns, tell them the warning in a line, with its at; call push with force: true and that at only once their message is just "push anyway". In any other turn it pushes nothing. Post, approve, merge, close or push only with these tools, never with gh, gh api or git push in your shell.",
    "name": "push",
    "presentation": null,
  },
]
`;
